  "narration": {
    "_intro": "Welcome to Apple Farm House, a single-storey home of timber and board-marked concrete set in an orchard valley near Pohang. This tour is rebuilt from the architect's plan and published photos.",
    "entrance": "You arrive under the folded concrete canopy. The entrance hall keeps shoes and coats out of the living space; its finishes weren't photographed, so they're estimated.",
    "kitchen": "The kitchen and dining area share one long room with the living space. A white gloss kitchen wraps the corner under a window, with a solid oak table beneath twin pendants.",
    "living": "The living room is lined in oak and birch plywood under a slatted timber ceiling. A full-height built-in runs the north wall, and wide timber-framed glazing opens to the deck.",
    "deck": "The deck steps straight out from the living room toward the fields and the mountains beyond.",
    "corridor": "A quiet corridor of board-marked concrete leads to the private wing: the guest room, the bathroom and the master bedroom at the far end.",
    "master": "The master bedroom sits at the west end with a long wardrobe wall. It wasn't photographed, so its layout follows the plan and its finishes are estimated.",
    "bathroom": "The bathroom follows the plan's layout of basin, WC and shower. It wasn't photographed, so these finishes are estimated.",
    "guest": "The guest room has a wardrobe wall and a long low window to the south. It wasn't photographed, so its finishes are estimated.",
    "utility": "The utility room behind the kitchen holds laundry and storage. It's shown from the plan only."
  }
